# Organisation creation and member addition examples

## 1. Create organisation

Test organisations doivent être soit des groupes de vente, soit des structures de prestation de service.

POST /api/organisations?ownerId=1

Request body (groupe de vente):

{
  "owner_id": 1,
  "name": "Groupe de vente Gold",
  "type": "SALES_GROUP",
  "category": "PRIVATE",
  "public_join": false,
  "requires_approval": true,
  "restricted_toAdmins_only": false
}

Expected response (201 Created):

{
  "id": 101,
  "owner_id": 1,
  "name": "Groupe de vente Gold",
  "type": "SALES_GROUP",
  "category": "PRIVATE",
  "public_join": false,
  "requires_approval": true,
  "restricted_toAdmins_only": false,
  "created_at": "2026-07-20T12:00:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-07-20T12:00:00"
}

Request body (prestation de service):

{
  "owner_id": 1,
  "name": "Réseau de prestation Gold",
  "type": "DISTRIBUTION_NETWORK",
  "category": "PUBLIC",
  "public_join": true,
  "requires_approval": false,
  "restricted_toAdmins_only": false
}

Expected response (201 Created):

{
  "id": 102,
  "owner_id": 1,
  "name": "Réseau de prestation Gold",
  "type": "DISTRIBUTION_NETWORK",
  "category": "PUBLIC",
  "public_join": true,
  "requires_approval": false,
  "restricted_toAdmins_only": false,
  "created_at": "2026-07-20T12:05:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-07-20T12:05:00"
}

> Note: The controller uses the `ownerId` query parameter to identify the organisation owner. Including `owner_id` in the body is supported by the DTO, but the request path must also include `?ownerId=1`.

Swagger example (OpenAPI): assurez-vous que l'exemple de corps inclut `owner_id` et que la requête fournit `ownerId` en query. Exemple d'entrée pour Swagger UI:

Request URL (example): `/api/organisations?ownerId=1`

Request body (Swagger example):

{
  "owner_id": 1,
  "name": "Groupe de vente Gold",
  "type": "SALES_GROUP",
  "category": "PRIVATE",
  "public_join": false,
  "requires_approval": true,
  "restricted_toAdmins_only": false
}

Si votre Swagger/OpenAPI montre seulement `ownerId` en query et lève une erreur "For 'ownerId': Required field is not provided", fournissez aussi `owner_id` dans l'exemple de corps pour que la validation passe via les deux chemins.

## 2. Add organisation members

POST /api/orgmembers/101/members

Example 1: Add user 4 as full member

Request body:

{
  "userId": 4,
  "type": "FULL_MEMBER",
  "roles": ["ROLE_USER"]
}

Expected response (200 OK):

{
  "id": {
    "organisationId": 101,
    "userId": 4
  },
  "type": "FULL_MEMBER",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "joinedAt": "2026-07-20T12:01:00",
  "modifiedAt": "2026-07-20T12:01:00",
  "roles": ["ROLE_USER"]
}

Example 2: Add user 5 as admin member

Request body:

{
  "userId": 5,
  "type": "ADMIN",
  "roles": ["ROLE_ADMIN", "ROLE_USER"]
}

Example 3: Add user 6 as read-only member

Request body:

{
  "userId": 6,
  "type": "VIEWER",
  "roles": ["ROLE_VIEWER"]
}

Example 4: Add user 7 as reviewer member

Request body:

{
  "userId": 7,
  "type": "REVIEWER",
  "roles": ["ROLE_REVIEWER", "ROLE_USER"]
}

